{"id": "EUVD-2026-53264", "enisaUuid": "26398c9b-a280-3a4d-9cea-492a2cf41b5b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: fix fils_discovery double free on alloc failure\n\nieee80211_set_fils_discovery() calls kfree_rcu() on the old template\nbefore allocating the replacement. If the kzalloc() then fails, it\nreturns -ENOMEM while link->u.ap.fils_discovery still points at the\nobject already queued for freeing. A later update or AP teardown\n(ieee80211_stop_ap()) re-queues that same rcu_head; the second free is\ncaught by KASAN when the RCU sheaf is processed in softirq:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: double-free in rcu_free_sheaf (mm/slub.c:5850)\n  Free of addr ffff88800c065280 by task swapper/0/0\n   ...\n   __rcu_free_sheaf_prepare (mm/slub.c:2634 mm/slub.c:2940)\n   rcu_free_sheaf (mm/slub.c:5850)\n   rcu_core (kernel/rcu/tree.c:2617 kernel/rcu/tree.c:2869)\n   handle_softirqs (kernel/softirq.c:622)\n  The buggy address belongs to the cache kmalloc-96 of size 96\n\nQueue the old object for kfree_rcu() only after the new one is published,\nmatching ieee80211_set_probe_resp() and ieee80211_set_s1g_short_beacon().", "datePublished": "2026-08-05T08:08:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:48:42", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2c55079155a953db669ca1986a985fa286bad95", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5baaa1042f71dd4b8e418f2cdd516808702d229b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1981fba71797ec95e6755fb882cad88899a2a84f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/286e52a799fa158bdbd77da1426c4d93f9a6e7ad"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5gxw-5rpr-7mcv", "CVE-2026-64570"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c126f82-67a4-3d64-9223-7dafc4b2ec72", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "47e78976-3c1a-371a-ac3f-cd9bb2d0b898", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b1c256eb4aedfc71dd97d5951ccff824b41d628 <5baaa1042f71dd4b8e418f2cdd516808702d229b"}, {"id": "59f8ce7e-3edd-3aaf-9a01-ea64d06e9349", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "67915071-d5f2-377c-a4be-23f4cf493e54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b1c256eb4aedfc71dd97d5951ccff824b41d628 <e2c55079155a953db669ca1986a985fa286bad95"}, {"id": "7445f502-4e38-39b4-aab1-299bd1c65e33", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "7ea45535-04a2-3c8c-81de-e117455bef30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}, {"id": "ab4ca075-2164-3c57-b628-2c8804132dfa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b1c256eb4aedfc71dd97d5951ccff824b41d628 <1981fba71797ec95e6755fb882cad88899a2a84f"}, {"id": "ab7b3fff-b268-37dc-b7c3-c54006368958", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "d1a7a523-6f79-313a-8d23-08984ea84381", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}, {"id": "e799baf2-28f3-35f4-bdd3-b408ec1684b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b1c256eb4aedfc71dd97d5951ccff824b41d628 <286e52a799fa158bdbd77da1426c4d93f9a6e7ad"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4616ad80-f3ac-3e5b-96d9-35512c6f8aa8", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}